# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DIGITAL TYPOLOGY — CANONICAL INTAKE, COMPILED TO AXIOM
# source   : Canonical_Intake.xml, process id "digital-typology" v2.0
#            (2026-10-08 clean: join = purpose/ef/ifd/provider/refs;
#            relation, verb, perspective, observation, non_goal removed;
#            continuous-audit rule removed; Collection concept added;
#            completion = an appropriately named core node)
# schema   : metaform.axiom — the schema; core node at root
# platform : Metaform MCP — intake{start,element,join,show,remove,finish}
# address  : logic.intake.typology (proposed) · entry: perform
# tool bindings (per the system-side gap list; fixes in progress there):
#   B1 ifd bound to the tool enum sends|receives|both (schema prints send|receive)
#   B2 intake start takes no id; {Id} travels in the finish report
#   B3 member paths land as refs on elements (sources layer); the join tool
#      carries no refs argument
#   B4 EXCL has no condition value; a note with no condition is currently
#      discarded, so exclude notes may be lost until the fix lands
#   B6 subtype joins removed (D115): an annealed part is recorded as an
#      ordinary join with the parent element as receiver
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@LEXICON — load-bearing. Every term resolves here and nowhere else.
  Core node := the project itself. An ELEMENT with a name and the namespace
          address core. It is not a type, so it takes no part in the namespace
          and is never reversed or read as one. Its job is connective:
          everything the intake records connects to it — the AUEs, the
          collections, and the CQUs. In the schema it is the single child
          of METAFORM(id, description): ELEMENT( name := canonical name |
          project name | inferred name ), holding everything.
  AUE  := Artifact Under Examination: the entity (thing or things) being
          examined, created, or used — photographs, contracts, stories,
          resale assets, software; one or many. Whether an AUE serves as
          an asset depends on its use in that context.
  Element := any nameable part of an entity, considered as a TYPE.
          Nameable ≠ notable: many elements are immediately seen or easily
          inferred and deserve no special attention.
  Entity := a whole, independent thing with its own distinct existence.
          Scope-relative: zooming into an element makes it an entity with
          subordinate elements of its own.
  Containment := Artifacts ⊂ Entities ⊂ Elements.
  Join := a dictionary object that exists in the RE; it contains a
          dictionary of objects containing type-specific or AUE-specific
          references and logic. The recorded bond is tripartite:
          RE —OP ↔ EF— PE, carried as purpose, ef, ifd, provider, with
          refs where required. Nothing else is the join.
  OP   := Operative Purpose — the WHY. The active goal held in the RE's
          join that an element's encounter function intends to accomplish.
  EF   := Encounter Function — the HOW of what is delivered: the mechanism,
          interface, relationship, or method through which a PE performs
          its purpose for its RE (the function of an encounter, or the
          encounter of a function, per the artifact's context — the
          Unloaded Definition; the context resolves the sense). The EF
          belongs to the PE but is stored in the RE-owned join, because one
          PE type may satisfy different REs' OPs through different EFs.
          !> Never a single element-level EF record outside its joins.
  RE   := Receiving Element/Entity — the WHO or WHAT bearing an OP. The OP
          belongs to the receiver, and the join that records it lives in
          that receiver.
  CQU  := Cestui Que Use — the explicit RE that benefits from work on this
          TYPE of artifact and drives the most improvement in it. A party
          TYPE outside the AUE (human or organization), NEVER an element
          of the AUE. Receives the root join. Recorded under {CQU_Base}.
          Every CQU is an RE; most REs are not CQUs.
  PE   := Providing Element — the join's other endpoint: whatever's EF
          fulfills the RE's OP. NOT a role attribute. The same element may
          bear an OP as an RE in one join and provide an EF as a PE in
          another, without duplication.
  AT   := Artifact Type — a classification that anneals same-type AUEs
          (photos, data objects, scripts, templates) into one type.
  Collection := a namespace root for identifying sets. A collection groups
          AUEs of one content kind and sits above the AUE: its members are
          the artifacts under examination. Main use: projects that are many
          artifacts of a kind rather than one — a folder of photos, a body
          of contracts, a set of stories. A codebase is one artifact and
          normally needs no collection. The address after collection.
          mirrors the members' own type: collection.media.photo reads
          "photo media collection"; stripping collection. gives the
          members' type, so the address alone says what is in the set.
          Narrows the same way: collection.media.photo.product. Normal
          namespace rules apply. Each collection can have a distinct CQU
          with its own tripartite root join, so one project can hold
          several roots of purpose, one per collection, under the core
          node. Member paths are refs on the collection element (sources
          layer), each member keeping its identity through its ref;
          downstream, tagged refs allow automated collection and
          organization while retaining the file paths or extraction, and
          the collection address is what knowledge layers, workflows, and
          work can target.
  NE   := Notable Element — states an essential external demand or
          dependency: what the system explicitly expects, needs, or
          depends on from its environment to operate.
  DE   := Defining Element — the notable element whose loss would prevent
          the AUE from remaining the same type. Its EF serves the OP of a
          CQU outside this AUE and names the AUE's functional type as the
          converged result of its functionality — expressed independently
          of medium, encoding, genre, and style.
  SE   := Substantial Element — an element whose EF helps the DE serve the
          CQU's OP. Substantial for what it is MEANT to contribute, even
          when that contribution is subversive, weak, replaceable, or
          should be improved.
  Parametric := a tunable quality or quantity carrying no name of its own
          in this AUE's namespace scope. Never named, never addressed,
          never an NE, never part of intake — no matter how many exist.

@STATE_INIT:
  {Prompt}    := PARAM = this project folder's contexts
                 — a stated target or a task; prompts may refine the run:
                 refinement, correction-layer construction, blind-spot
                 analysis, new features/enhancements, or any user purpose.
  {Id}        := GENERATE now — nothing in this run points to it; it exists
                 so this result can later be pasted into
                 digital-typology-expand, whose deep_result links back via
                 a matching ref. Travels in the finish report (B2).
  {Roots}     := code | document | media | data | upstream | downstream
                 | collection
  {CQU_Base}  := downstream.cqu
  {Marks}     := MISS → condition=unbuilt (intended functionality absent)
               | BKN  → condition=broken  (code incorrect or not working)
               | EXCL → note="exclude: <why>" (appears not to belong; for
                 examination — no condition value exists for it; B4)
               | stage → condition=unbuilt | under-construction | built
                 (facts about a part on its way to existing; the intake
                 sets stages as it maps)
  {Phase}     := LOAD
  {Schema}    := {Metaform_Schema}  — metaform.axiom; bound at RECORD

@RECORD — binding to the intake tools; one object per call, AS REASONED,
          never holding the map until the end:
  START       := intake start()            — resume or fresh (B2: no id)
  ELEMENT(e)  := intake element( namespace_address, name_length, name,
                   role ∈ AUE|CQU|DE|SE|NE, condition?, note?, refs? )
                 — refs = [{key,value}]; member paths key="path",
                   value="[relative path]" (written to the sources layer)
  JOIN(j)     := intake join( receiver, elements=[PE addresses], purpose,
                   ef, ifd ∈ sends|receives|both, condition?, note? )
                 — the join carries exactly these; marks ride condition/note
  READBACK    := intake show( receiver? )
  REMOVE      := intake remove( receiver?, provider?, namespace_address? )
  FINISH      := intake finish( report, feedback? ) — report carries {Id}
  — re-recording an element or a join replaces the fields given and keeps
    the rest; a join recorded again with a held element adds new elements.

@CONSTRAINT:
  — the trace itself
  +> LOAD-BEARING: trace strictly the shape of the artifact's FUNCTION,
     traversing latent-space understanding of functionality only.
  !> Genre, medium, encoding, language, style, subject, or any variant
     that does not describe functionality — never on a leaf, never a
     basis for deeper intake.
  !> Do not assume you understand the intent before reading the intent.
  !> Do not assume the artifact is code; it may be a novel, documents,
     photos. If it is code, understand it deeply; that is not wasted.
  +> Artifacts may not exist yet, in part or at all: map the understanding,
     express what you don't see but infer should exist (condition=unbuilt),
     and mark drift where something doesn't match intent.
  !> Never solve a problem found; mark it ({Marks}) and move on.
  +> You are an archeologist of encounter, purpose, and function, and a
     forward scout: agents come in behind you blind. Create only what is
     long-lived and foundational — road signs and open lots where memories,
     knowledge, medium, style, and deeper intent can live and prompts can
     point.
  !> Never say in words what can change tomorrow; point with refs.
  ~> Every word beyond the expression of the system's function costs every
     agent after you. Saying more on one thing is not helping; saying less
     on many things is.
  — elements and joins
  +> Elements are discrete functional roles actively instantiated by this
     artifact, named at their most specific reusable TYPE level.
  !> Vague top-level labels where a specific functional mechanism exists.
  +> Namespace identity stays type-level; the joins carry the AUE-specific
     Operative Purpose, Encounter Function, and refs where present.
     Address general; join specific.
  +> A join speaks about this artifact, in its own particulars. Where the
     AUE represents something, describe the function of that representation
     within the AUE — never substitute the real-world functionality of the
     thing represented.
  +> refs on a join only when it needs type- or artifact-specific
     references or logic beyond purpose and ef.
  +> For every AUE, seek SE elements.
  +> Focus on notable elements; nameable ≠ notable.
  +> Seek a thorough, complete map of the parent functionalities; keep the
     graph's shape limited to functional elements as types while the joins
     speak to the function of the AUE as a whole.
  — identity, roles, and the map's shape
  +> An element's identity is its namespace_address, not its readable
     name. "tool registry" is prose; code.registry.tool is the element.
     Every reference to an element uses the address; a name with no
     matching address references nothing.
  +> An element's address must never be prefixed by the AUE's address just
     because the AUE contains it: code.store, not code.map.functional.store.
     Containment is shown by the structure (elements nested in the AUE,
     joins in their receivers), never by the address. The project is not a
     type of anything; it is what holds the types together — the core node.
  +> One role per element inside the AUE: DE, SE, or NE. A CQU outside
     the AUE carries role CQU and never an AUE role. PE is not a role.
  +> Project elements remain under code|document|media|data regardless of
     join role.
  +> upstream.* links external code|document|media|data providing into the
     project; downstream.cqu.* links external CQUs; other downstream.*
     entries link external receivers. Boundary links, not join-direction
     namespaces: never decomposed, never traced into, hold no project
     elements beneath them.
  — process discipline
  +> Intake is never gated or judged; only the resulting map may be graded
     and the intake refined contextually afterward.
  +> Record each element and join the moment it is reasoned, one object
     per call ({RECORD}).
  +> An element is written in full where it first appears; on reappearance
     it carries namespace_address, name_length, name, role only.
  +> The platform's active module instructions (memory retrieval before
     work, durable findings at the narrowest node, task tracking) remain
     in force throughout.

@NAMESPACE — a typological ontology, NOT a taxonomy. No filler segments
             (domain, class); no segment minimum or maximum.
  +> REVERSIBILITY: periods→spaces, segments reversed, reads as a
     well-understood, inferenceable noun; a child takes its parent's name
     as its last name when reversed.
  +> PROPER NOUN: each entry names a type of functional approach.
  +> NARROWING: trunk to leaf; each entry is its parent type, or a
     function within it — never a non-functionality.
  +> SEGMENTATION: words forming a valid prefix of their own stay separate
     segments (code.engine.game, code.engine.physics); underscore-join
     within one segment only when none does (code.queue.dead_letter,
     data.bill_of_materials), and the result must still read correctly
     reversed.
  +> name_length := lookback segment count forming the well-understood
     short name.
  +> GENERAL/SPECIFIC: the address names the TYPE and stays general; the
     join stays specific.
  +> LEXICON: established practitioner terminology; where no standard term
     exists, the plain common noun for what the thing functionally is or
     does. !> NEVER coin, invent, or adapt a term. No abstract pattern
     labels, bespoke synonyms, shorthand, colloquial or marketing terms.
  +> name := the canonical name exactly as the project specifications use
     it; absent a specification, the industry term.
  REFERENCE:
    code.engine.game ✔ (runtime a game runs on: main loop, rendering,
      input, simulation — independent of genre; known by that exact name)
    code.engine.game.fps ✔ (proof: first-person camera + targeting reticle)
    code.engine.game.platformer ✘ — defines the fundamental challenge and
      objective of a game, not a technical functionality; proof: spatial
      navigation and overcoming environmental obstacles.
      *Load-bearing invalid example.*
    code.game ✘ (not a function)    code.game.engine ✘ (subject variant;
      invalid parent)               code.cpp ✘ (language)
    media.photo.jpg ✘ (encoding)    document.word.story.conflict ✘ (encoding)
    document.story.conflict ✔   media.image ✔   media.asset.image ✔
    media.photo ✔   media.photo.scenery ✔ (function of an encounter: the
      scene is the focus; its subject is not the DE)
    collection.media.photo ✔ ("photo media collection"; strip collection.
      → the members' type)   collection.media.photo.product ✔
  READING: code.loop.main → "main loop program code";
           code.bus.data.event → "event data bus code".

@CQU_RULES — deciding the CQU takes deep consideration: it is not present
             in what you examine. Infer it from what the artifact IS.
  +> Assume the artifact is converted into a metaform to be improved. The
     CQUs that matter are those whose purpose drives changes or
     improvements; enumerate each. The one driving the MOST improvement
     gives the best inference.
  +> The CQU forms the tripartite root join that makes the map artifact-
     specific: CQU as receiver, its OP as the why, the PE's EF as the how.
     Every other join traces back to a root join through its receivers.
  +> Each collection can have a distinct CQU with its own root join, so
     one project can hold several roots of purpose, one per collection.
  +> Elements are types, so the CQU is a type: the party type holding an
     objective purpose for this type of object, at its most specific
     reusable level. When one person holds several roles, name the role
     that changes the artifact, by the title that role carries.
  !> Never the person who asked for the intake. Never the operator. Never
     "End User" (a non-answer). Never "developer" unless the type is
     code.ide or an actual programming tool.
  CALIBRATION:
    media.photo → seller ✔ (presents the photo its best to drive a sale)
    media.photo → social media poster ✔ · blogger ✔ (drive changes)
    media.photo → buyer ✘ (judges; judging doesn't improve)
    media.photo → insurance company ✘ (records; wants it unchanged)
    media.photo → operator ✘ (true of every artifact; identifies nothing)
    document.story → Reader ✔ (vested — their time — in the story being
      good; vested does not always mean money)

@CONDITION (PHASES):
  {Phase} := LOAD      — context not yet clicked
           | SURVEY    — context loaded; members not yet all observed
           | GROUP     — members observed; collections / ATs / root joins
                         not recorded
           | DECOMPOSE — root joins recorded; DEs not yet opened as REs
           | TRACE     — unsatisfied OPs or unnamed NEs remain
           | CLOSURE   — trace ended; coverage not yet proven total
           | ANNEAL    — coverage total; shape not yet converged
           | PROOF     — shape converged; map not yet proofed whole
           | FINISH    — proofed; not yet finished

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH ({Phase}):
    | [LOAD]      -> P_Load
    | [SURVEY]    -> P_Survey
    | [GROUP]     -> P_Group
    | [DECOMPOSE] -> P_Decompose
    | [TRACE]     -> P_Trace
    | [CLOSURE]   -> P_Closure
    | [ANNEAL]    -> P_Anneal
    | [PROOF]     -> P_Proof
    | [FINISH]    -> P_Finish

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Load):                                   — step 1
  1. ∇({Prompt}) => resolve the target; absent a stated one, this project
     folder's contexts. START.
  2. ∇(target) => load context the way you understand your own system
     prompt, until things click and you can see the forest for the trees.
     Read the intent before judging anything against it.
  3. Δ => form the model of what you expect to see; note what you infer
     should exist but don't see; note drift. You are finding understanding,
     not building the project. {Phase} := SURVEY.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Survey):                                 — steps 2–3
  1. FOR each member of the target (every member of a folder or collection
     before any grouping is finalized):
       ∇(member) => OBSERVE it; REASON its AT, its DE, its SE and NE
       elements, and the OP/EF relationships that distinguish its
       functionality.
  2. Throughout: vigilance for drift and apparent errors — between
     documentation, specifications, and code, in either direction. Record
     concerns at the unique element type each belongs to, with refs:
     MISS, BKN, EXCL per {Marks}. Record; never fix.
  3. Δ(all members) => {Phase} := GROUP.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Group):                                  — steps 3–4
  1. FOR each AUE: ORGANIZE members into AT groups capable of generating a
     useful imperative for an agent from (the OP of the CQU) and (the EF
     of the PE) of the AUE's DE in service of the CQU's OP as stakeholder.
     GROUP only members whose shared functionality supports the same
     AT-level imperative; retain member identity through refs.
  2. WHERE the project is many artifacts of one content kind (a folder of
     photos, a body of contracts, a set of stories — not a codebase, which
     is one artifact): RECORD the set at collection.<members' type>, its
     member AUE paths as refs on the collection element, each member
     keeping its identity through its ref. The core node holds the
     collections; each collection holds its AUEs. A single-artifact
     project: the core node holds the one AUE directly, no collection.
  3. FOR each AT / collection:
       a. ELEMENT( {CQU_Base}.<cqu type>, role=CQU ) per @CQU_RULES.
       b. JOIN( receiver={CQU address}, elements=[DE address],
                purpose=the CQU's OP, ef=the DE's EF for this encounter,
                ifd ) — the tripartite root join, one per collection where
                collections exist.
       c. Member paths: refs key="path" value="[relative path]" on the
          member elements (sources layer, B3).
       d. CHECK BKN; CHECK MISS.
  4. Δ => {Phase} := DECOMPOSE.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Decompose):                              — step 5
  1. FOR each AUE, FOR each AT:
       ∇(DE as RE) => DECOMPOSE its requirements and dependencies as EFs
       of other elements. The DE simultaneously remains the PE serving the
       external CQU's OP where that relationship exists.
       IF an encountered element itself bears an OP -> TRACE it as an RE;
       no duplicate namespace record (re-record carries address,
       name_length, name, role only).
       CHECK BKN; CHECK MISS.
  2. Δ => {Phase} := TRACE.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Trace):                                  — steps 6–9
  1. FOR each element whose EF serves the intent of an OP:
       JOIN( receiver = the RE, elements = [the PE's address],
             purpose  = the active OP statement,
             ef       = the Providing Element's Encounter Function,
             ifd      = the primary flow of information: sends from the OP
                        to the EF, receives from the EF to the OP, both
                        for equal need,
             refs where needed )
       RECORD as reasoned, one object at a time. CHECK BKN; CHECK MISS.
  2. RECURSE from the element named in the first OP; MOVE to the next
     element; TREAT it as an RE where it bears requirements or an OP of
     its own.
  3. FOR that element: FIND its OPs — what it needs and wants from the
     rest of the AUE, or from outside it (upstream.*), to deliver its own
     EF. Element functionality serves the OP of entities, so every OP
     found traces back through its receivers to the OP of the external CQU.
  4. CONTINUE UNTIL no unsatisfied OPs remain, and no NEs of this AUE must
     be named to understand the artifact. Parametrics are never NEs and
     never enter intake.
  5. Δ => {Phase} := CLOSURE.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Closure):                                — step 10
  1. RETURN to the survey of P_Load/P_Survey. No aspect of the AUE's
     functionality is left out:
     FOR each functionality the trace has not reached:
       FIND the RE whose OP it serves; RECORD the join.
       WHERE it is only a part of a functionality already named, the
       parent's join states it — no new record.
  2. Δ => {Phase} := ANNEAL.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Anneal):                                 — step 11
  1. Wherever possible, AGGREGATE PE subfunctions into an RE's parent
     function by mapping their shared integration joins. ANNEAL and
     COMBINE elements into a macro-function, ENCAPSULATING subparts that
     share the same join.
  2. ENCAPSULATE a subpart ONLY WHEN the parent's purpose can carry its
     purpose; otherwise KEEP it as an independent functional element.
  3. KEEP each encapsulated subpart's purpose as a refinement of the
     parent's, recorded one level deeper: a JOIN with the element it is
     part of as receiver — an ordinary join per D115 (B6), never a
     separate top-level element.
  4. LET the purpose join carry the combined encounter; optimize no
     functionality away. An absorbed subpart stays an element, held by
     the parent's join; it is never removed.
  5. Δ => {Phase} := PROOF.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Proof):                                  — step 12
  1. READBACK the recorded map whole (intake show).
  2. CHECK it against the artifact AND against this document.
  3. CORRECT it (remove / re-record; replacements carry only the fields
     that change). ANNEAL it. COMPLETE it.
  4. Δ => {Phase} := FINISH.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (P_Finish):
  1. FINISH( report = {Id} + the project report: broken code, things
     needing fixing, anything not or partially working — the MISS/BKN/EXCL
     marks with their elements and refs;
     feedback = Metaform-process feedback where you have it: bad
     semantics, tool/schema mismatch, where you got stuck ).
  2. YIELD.

@VERIFY — the second, final pass; realize the load-bearing importance of
          the operation just performed:
  [1] An appropriately named core node contains all other elements —
      every element and join connects to it, every AUE reached from it
      directly or through its collection, nothing free-floating or
      disconnected?                                          NO -> P_Closure.
  [2] Every recorded OP traces back through its receivers to a CQU's root
      join at {CQU_Base}.*?                                  NO -> P_Trace.
  [3] Any element address prefixed by the AUE's address (containment
      encoded in the namespace)?                             YES -> P_Proof: correct per step 12.
  [4] Any leaf typed by genre, medium, encoding, language, style, or
      subject?                                               YES -> P_Proof: correct per step 12.
  [5] Any parametric named or enumerated?                    YES -> REMOVE it.
  [6] Any CQU recorded as an element of the AUE, or bearing an AUE role?
                                                             YES -> correct: role=CQU at {CQU_Base}.*.
  [7] Any element-level EF recorded outside a join?          YES -> move into its joins.
  [8] Every join carries exactly purpose, ef, ifd, and refs where
      required — nothing else?                               NO -> re-record the join.
  [9] Every element/join recorded as reasoned, one object per call, and
      re-appearances carried in short form?                  NO -> re-record correctly.
  [10] Problems marked, never solved?                        NO -> strip the fix; keep the mark.
  [11] Proof pass (P_Proof) performed against artifact AND this document?
                                                             NO -> P_Proof.
  ALL PASS -> P_Finish. YIELD.
